title: Polygon colliders
intro: A collider can now be any shape with straight sides: its points dragged, added and taken off in the Scene view or traced round a sprite, concave ones split into pieces by themselves, turning with a body that rotates.
project: Contraption | Polygons

# A new scene in the Contraption project (which has a ball picture, Textures/ball.png), its camera moved out to see it
# all: a floor 40 wide whose top is at y = -2.5.
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Polygons
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position = 0, 1, 0
set: Camera.Size = 7
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Floor
set: Transform.Position = 0, -3, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 40, 1
set: Sprite.Tint = #4A4E5A
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 40, 1
deselect

chapter: A hill | Points dragged in the Scene view
create: Empty
rename: Hill
set: Transform.Position = -4, -2.5, 0
add: PolygonCollider
set: PolygonCollider.Points = -3 0; 3 0; 0 2
expectcomponents: Hill = Transform, PolygonCollider
say: A polygon collider is a shape with straight sides between its points. Selected, each point has a knob, and each side a plus.
explain: handle:PolygonCollider.3 | A point | Drag a point's knob to move it; hold Ctrl to snap to half units.
path: PolygonCollider.3 = 0, 3
expectvalue: Hill.PolygonCollider.Points = -3 0; 3 0; 0 3
explain: handle:PolygonCollider.+2 | Add a point | Drag the plus on a side to add a point there.
path: PolygonCollider.+2 = 1.5, -0.8
expectvalue: Hill.PolygonCollider.Points = -3 0; 1.5 -0.8; 3 0; 0 3
say: That made it concave. It's split into convex pieces by itself, drawn faintly inside it, and collides as the shape it is.
removepoint: PolygonCollider.2
expectvalue: Hill.PolygonCollider.Points = -3 0; 3 0; 0 3
say: A double-click takes a point off again. Each change is one undo step.
set: PolygonCollider.Points = -3 0; 3 0; -3 1.5; 3 1.5
explain: component:PolygonCollider | Fixed up | Points that don't make a proper shape are fixed up and said so: these sides cross, so it's taken as the shape round all its points, drawn in red.
set: PolygonCollider.Points = -3 0; 3 0; 0 3
deselect

chapter: Turning with its body | A wedge that tips over
create: Empty
rename: Wedge
set: Transform.Position = -4, 2.5, 0
set: Transform.Rotation.Z = 20
add: PolygonCollider
set: PolygonCollider.Points = -0.6 -0.4; 0.6 -0.4; 0 0.6
add: Body
set: Body.Rotates = true
say: With a body that rotates, a polygon turns with its entity, round where it balances.
play
wait: 3
expectvalue: Wedge.Body.Asleep = true
explain: entity:Wedge | Resting | It fell on the hill, tipped over, slid off its slant and came to rest on one of its sides.
stop

chapter: Fitted to a sprite | Its outline traced
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Rock
set: Transform.Position = 3, 3, 0
pickimage: Sprite.Image = Textures/ball.png
set: Sprite.Size = 1.2, 1.2
add: BoxCollider
menu: Entity > Fit Polygon Collider to Sprite
expectcomponents: Rock = Transform, Sprite, PolygonCollider
explain: component:PolygonCollider | Traced | Fit Polygon Collider to Sprite traced round the picture, in place of its box: a dozen points hugging it.
add: Body
set: Body.Rotates = true
play
wait: 4
expectvalue: Rock.Body.Asleep = true
explain: entity:Rock | Rests on its side | It landed on one of its sides and stays there, as the shape it is.
stop
